From 9c16795c4639b6b134104e9881983987efb4d35a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:31:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 70/70] ppc32: no lock-free TimeTicks atomic on 32-bit PowerPC

First G5 cycle of the 14.6 port, parade #3 (heap.cc at first; the same
header is reached by memory-allocator.cc, memory-pool.cc,
isolate-group.cc, allocation.cc and accounting-allocator.cc):

  src/heap/memory-pool.h:254:47: error: static assertion failed
    static_assert(std::atomic<base::TimeTicks>::is_always_lock_free);

14.6's MemoryPool (new since 13.6, src/heap/memory-pool.h) remembers
when its delayed page-release task was last posted in a
std::atomic<base::TimeTicks>; TimeTicks is a single int64_t.  Same
class as 0050's two-word FreelistHead: upstream's 32-bit hosts make an
8-byte atomic lock-free (arm with ldrexd/strexd, ia32 with cmpxchg8b),
32-bit PowerPC does not - lwarx/stwcx. are word-sized and the baseline
is generic ppc - so gcc routes 8-byte atomics to libatomic's locked
implementation and is_always_lock_free is false.  Drop the assert on
that host: the two accesses (a relaxed store in PostDelayedReleaseTask,
a relaxed load in PostDelayedReleaseTaskIfNeeded) compile unchanged
against libatomic's locked 8-byte load/store (-latomic is already on
the link line for 0036's SharedArrayBuffer i64 atomics and 0050), the
timestamp is still read and written whole.  V8_HOST_ARCH_* reach this
header through mutex.h -> lazy-instance.h -> macros.h -> logging.h ->
build_config.h, as 0050's reach segmented-table.h via globals.h.

Class check: is_always_lock_free / is_lock_free() / ATOMIC_*_LOCK_FREE
appear at exactly two sites in v8/src + v8/include at 14.6 - this one
and 0050's; none in third_party.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 v8/src/heap/memory-pool.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/src/heap/memory-pool.h b/v8/src/heap/memory-pool.h
index 89a4609..d081b49 100644
--- a/v8/src/heap/memory-pool.h
+++ b/v8/src/heap/memory-pool.h
@@ -251,7 +251,13 @@ class MemoryPool final {
   std::atomic<base::TimeTicks> posted_time_;
   std::unique_ptr<CancelableTaskManager> cancellable_task_manager_;
 
+#if V8_HOST_ARCH_PPC && V8_HOST_ARCH_32_BIT
+  // TimeTicks is one int64_t; 32-bit PowerPC has no 64-bit reservation pair
+  // (lwarx/stwcx. are word-sized), so posted_time_ goes through libatomic's
+  // locked fallback instead, like the segmented-table freelist head.
+#else
   static_assert(std::atomic<base::TimeTicks>::is_always_lock_free);
+#endif
 };
 
 }  // namespace v8::internal
